#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203803 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0afa4d8-6d02-52c6-9836-12089de8f406" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Given a Dataset or Summary Statistics"}] :question/id #uuid "6f0e3d4b-943b-5710-a996-ac4d3c68778d" :question/math-academy-id "e-16399" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\, x_i \\,$** | $15$ | $12$ | $13$ | $16$ | $19$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\, y_i \\,$** | $8$ | $13$ | $6$ | $15$ | $13$ |\n\nCalculate $S_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n},$ $S_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of $x_i$ and $y_i$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample means $\\overline{x}$ and $\\overline{y}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{15+12+13+16+19}{5} = 15\n$$\n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{8+13+6+15+13}{5} = 11\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the $x_i$ and $\\overline{x}$, $y_i$ and $\\overline{y}$, and their product.\n\n| **$\\, x_i \\,$** | $15$ | $12$ | $13$ | $16$ | $19$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\, y_i \\,$** | $8$ | $13$ | $6$ | $15$ | $13$ |\n| **$\\, (x_i - \\overline{x}) \\,$** | $0$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| **$\\, (y_i - \\overline{y}) \\,$** | $-3$ | $2$ | $-5$ | $4$ | $2$ |\n| **$\\, (x_i - \\overline{x})(y_i - \\overline{y}) \\,$** | $0$ | $-6$ | $10$ | $4$ | $8$ |\n\nTherefore, $S_{xy}$ is\n\n$$\nS_{xy} = 0 + (-6) + 10 + 4 + 8 = 16.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203804 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204011 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83df73fc-c0cc-5605-9b39-453de0c37cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating S(x,y) Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "489e5ffd-9e78-567b-b009-25d0c004825a" :question/math-academy-id "e-16400" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $30$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{30},$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{30}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{x}_{i}=315, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{y}_{i}=278, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=2\\,964.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDetermine $S_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n},$ the statistic $S_{xy}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & =2\\,964-\\frac{1}{30}(315)(278) \\\\  & =2\\,964-2\\,919 \\\\  & =45.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203805 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "714000f9-caea-57a3-a8cb-6b8ec99960d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Variance and Covariance"}] :question/id #uuid "7daa2313-4672-5624-aac2-e3b87b6ec366" :question/math-academy-id "e-16401" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $35$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{35},$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{35}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=35,\\,{S}_{yy}=133,\\,{S}_{xy}=105.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\mathrm{Cov}(x, y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n},$ their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $S_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of $x_i$ and $y_i$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that $S_{xy} = 105.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{105}{35} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203806 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f0ed04b-f011-5818-952d-425a19e0cd5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "9804df95-f494-5d99-acbd-97c69344d401" :question/math-academy-id "e-16402" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\, x_i \\,$** | $10$ | $9$ | $8$ | $8$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\, y_i \\,$** | $15$ | $12$ | $14$ | $12$ | $8$ |\n\nGiven that $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^5 x_i^2 = 334,$ calculate $S_{xx}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data $x_i$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the $x_i$ data:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^n x_i = 10 + 9 + 8 + 8 + 5 = 40.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^5 x_i^2 = 334.$\n\nFinally, by substituting into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\nS_{xx} =334 - \\dfrac{1}{5}(40)^2 = 334- 320 = 14.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204443 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0afa4d8-6d02-52c6-9836-12089de8f406" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Given a Dataset or Summary Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b29b1a12-d0eb-5f2b-ab35-13a210b0d87d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b29b1a12-d0eb-5f2b-ab35-13a210b0d87d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512520} :answer-field/id #uuid "67543802-7a9b-5136-8b6c-fb241a29ee8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202599}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "afc7ddce-cfae-538b-a2da-388062ae3528" :question/math-academy-id "q-251486" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $8$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{8},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{8}.$\n\nYou are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}=1.6, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2}=5.1, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})=2.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, ${S}_{xy}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given statistics, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =2.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0afa4d8-6d02-52c6-9836-12089de8f406" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Given a Dataset or Summary Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f7ff9cc-ab5d-5741-b725-e396183c6acb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512165} {:answer/id #uuid "8e91a02b-fc69-5e88-9774-ad00afc6e6ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512434} {:answer/id #uuid "9a918d1e-73e9-5c1c-bc54-cf85f315a090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512465} {:answer/id #uuid "b8d3c88f-96c7-55f4-a69d-a68bc5f64a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512539} {:answer/id #uuid "e949b957-3ab5-5b0a-bdc3-5aaf0dc73ccb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f7ff9cc-ab5d-5741-b725-e396183c6acb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512165} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c725d7d-b2fd-5e71-9b0d-3ba4a9496550" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de5cf12f-ad3f-5f2c-aa7f-2181f5de72bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-251488" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $5$ | $11$ | $9$ | $12$ | $18$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $16$ | $14$ | $23$ | $17$ | $15$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{yy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{yy}$ is the sum of the squared deviations of the data ${y}_{i}$ from the mean $\\overset{―}{y},$ that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{yy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample mean $\\overset{―}{y}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{16+14+23+17+15}{5}=17.\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${y}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}$, and their squares.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $5$ | $11$ | $9$ | $12$ | $18$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $16$ | $14$ | $23$ | $17$ | $15$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-1$ | $-3$ | $6$ | $0$ | $-2$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2}\\,$** | $1$ | $9$ | $36$ | $0$ | $4$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{yy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{yy}=1+9+36+0+4=50.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204011 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83df73fc-c0cc-5605-9b39-453de0c37cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating S(x,y) Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44123af5-e2fd-5ea4-88e9-b70e9b3b267f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=85.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512240} {:answer/id #uuid "b32a8445-2ca4-5860-9a66-a3720ee75b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=41.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512522} {:answer/id #uuid "b564aa2d-1815-5b26-8895-65a367b53773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512529} {:answer/id #uuid "f38077d2-538a-52de-80fc-f81b787769d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512689} {:answer/id #uuid "ffef375f-eee1-5328-8ca8-8a877b28f600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffef375f-eee1-5328-8ca8-8a877b28f600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512721} :answer-field/id #uuid "880bbb07-a5bf-59b4-b7df-bceda5d80f95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3afcb82f-1e68-5666-b8c9-5cc1b12c399d" :question/math-academy-id "q-251493" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $6$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $2$ | $3$ | $9$ | $7$ | $5$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $16$ | $15$ | $14$ | $23$ | $18$ | $15$ |\n\nGiven that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=514,$ calculate ${S}_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of products of deviations from the means can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} & =2+3+9+7+5+4=30, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} & =16+15+14+23+18+15=101\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=514.$\n\nFinally, substituting in the above formula we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=514-\\frac{1}{6}(30)(101)=514-505=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "714000f9-caea-57a3-a8cb-6b8ec99960d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Variance and Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6de24c50-5265-5364-9820-9c85e283b7fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6de24c50-5265-5364-9820-9c85e283b7fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512360} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3a9827c-70b6-579a-935a-7abd7d1f3f4c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202613}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "afdb8bbd-524e-51f7-9c62-e82eb0471ab9" :question/math-academy-id "q-251494" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $25$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{25},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{25}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=125,\\,{S}_{yy}=37,\\,{S}_{xy}=64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, ${\\sigma }_{x}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the variance of ${x}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{x}^{2} & =\\frac{{S}_{xx}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xx}$ is the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${x}_{i}.$\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xx}=125.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{x}^{2} & =\\frac{125}{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204011 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83df73fc-c0cc-5605-9b39-453de0c37cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating S(x,y) Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53c4e854-a95f-58d6-aaed-933846604762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53c4e854-a95f-58d6-aaed-933846604762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512286} :answer-field/id #uuid "be6a6eec-8d66-5b27-9486-87b9b28cd48f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae961e11-0326-56d9-bf54-b78685d8bc1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-251795" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $16$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{16},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{16}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{16}{x}_{i}=168, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{16}{y}_{i}=158, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{16}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=1\\,742.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, ${S}_{xy}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the statistic ${S}_{xy}$ be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & =1\\,742-\\frac{1}{16}(168)(158) \\\\  & =1\\,742-1\\,659 \\\\  & =83.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512911 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204011 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83df73fc-c0cc-5605-9b39-453de0c37cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating S(x,y) Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a460ce37-c540-5545-a521-e22107bb905d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a460ce37-c540-5545-a521-e22107bb905d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512485} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b264c3d-9a36-5510-bb44-273869121f99" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91b1cdc3-3a29-5654-81e4-e52f93ca5959" :question/math-academy-id "q-251797" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $36$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{36},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{36}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{36}{x}_{i}=202, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{36}{y}_{i}=225, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{36}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=1\\,329.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,  ${S}_{xy}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the statistic ${S}_{xy}$ be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & =1\\,329-\\frac{1}{36}(202)(225) \\\\  & =1\\,329-1\\,262.5 \\\\  & =66.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204011 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83df73fc-c0cc-5605-9b39-453de0c37cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating S(x,y) Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18636295-8de4-5069-bf45-99f931c91f77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=104" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512155} {:answer/id #uuid "213dd1f5-d9c2-5866-9c88-a69119799bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512170} {:answer/id #uuid "34c23cc0-8a0e-5b53-8adb-9d28c46036b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=99" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512216} {:answer/id #uuid "441033b0-29be-53cb-a061-d8944e71cafe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=116" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512239} {:answer/id #uuid "55db0d56-f10f-55c9-b3b1-e5ac9217199a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "441033b0-29be-53cb-a061-d8944e71cafe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=116" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512239} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dfae525-f861-54d8-9ee3-bf782c835dce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f3d0803-8d23-5ea9-98da-36f1c313a55f" :question/math-academy-id "q-251803" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $7$ paired observations in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $9$ | $11$ | $12$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $3$ | $9$ | $27$ | $2$ | $4$ | $8$ | $1$ |\n\nGiven that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=494,$ calculate ${S}_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of products of deviations from the means can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} & =9+11+12+4+3+2+8=49, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} & =3+9+27+2+4+8+1=54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=494.$\n\nFinally, by substituting in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=494-\\frac{1}{7}(49)(54)=494-378=116.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204011 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83df73fc-c0cc-5605-9b39-453de0c37cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating S(x,y) Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0359330d-c81f-5a2c-9bd7-99ff4a75ee26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=5.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512107} {:answer/id #uuid "0368f1e8-5206-5cbe-b027-c81a9259238d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=4.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512108} {:answer/id #uuid "68426059-edda-5ec7-b81c-b4828febf565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=2.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512348} {:answer/id #uuid "826b8658-0dab-5fb2-a9bb-d4c31367b40c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=1.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512403} {:answer/id #uuid "b441c8c2-4523-544b-a9f9-830bb40032b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=6.50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68426059-edda-5ec7-b81c-b4828febf565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=2.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512348} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e4a57a7-76d3-509f-b185-ccce57c3cc55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c92a6a30-c262-56d7-be68-e946a5d2130d" :question/math-academy-id "q-251804" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $8$ paired observations in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $8$ | $6$ | $10$ | $5$ | $1$ | $12$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $2$ | $4$ | $5$ | $7$ | $1$ | $6$ | $11$ | $6$ |\n\nGiven that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=260,$ calculate ${S}_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of products of deviations from the means can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} & =8+6+10+5+1+12+4+3=49, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} & =2+4+5+7+1+6+11+6=42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=260.$\n\nFinally, by substituting in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=260-\\frac{1}{8}(49)(42)=260-257.25=2.75.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512868 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0afa4d8-6d02-52c6-9836-12089de8f406" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Given a Dataset or Summary Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "306f544b-90da-5c78-b553-0d134db9de1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=15.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512208} {:answer/id #uuid "afde0403-99c2-50a7-a1c1-6ebf58f5a1c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=21.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512513} {:answer/id #uuid "b059aaf0-3095-568d-a33a-3b5bbaa29fd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=25.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512514} {:answer/id #uuid "b8fe5882-4034-5822-be4d-7116344ced62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=19.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512541} {:answer/id #uuid "f071037e-24dc-56ef-ba11-564becd044e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=17.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f071037e-24dc-56ef-ba11-564becd044e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=17.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512681} :answer-field/id #uuid "644ff868-6cbb-5492-a503-41cd22bf83f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0adf3af5-290b-57ec-82ed-01a980659e66" :question/math-academy-id "q-251840" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $6$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $22$ | $24$ | $25$ | $23$ | $21$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $13$ | $15$ | $16$ | $18$ | $14$ | $17$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{yy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{yy}$ is the sum of the squared deviations of the data ${y}_{i}$ from the mean $\\overset{―}{y},$ that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{yy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample mean $\\overset{―}{y}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{13+15+16+18+14+17}{6}=15.5\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${y}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}$, and their squares.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $22$ | $24$ | $25$ | $23$ | $21$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $13$ | $15$ | $16$ | $18$ | $14$ | $17$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-2.5$ | $-0.5$ | $0.5$ | $2.5$ | $-1.5$ | $1.5$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2}\\,$** | $6.25$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ | $6.25$ | $2.25$ | $2.25$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{yy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{yy}=6.25+0.25+0.25+6.25+2.25+2.25=17.5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0afa4d8-6d02-52c6-9836-12089de8f406" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Given a Dataset or Summary Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02ba762e-68dd-5d26-8285-bcf47017e5d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xx}=42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512105} {:answer/id #uuid "0794d8af-bca9-5a3d-bc61-0e003ff578f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xx}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512119} {:answer/id #uuid "1b0ceb8d-eb40-573a-882e-15390e89900e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xx}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512158} {:answer/id #uuid "75fa1cbb-8b23-5647-9b66-e2abd16dba91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xx}=52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512378} {:answer/id #uuid "fd1e2e8e-b50d-56ed-b450-33a47d516b05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xx}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75fa1cbb-8b23-5647-9b66-e2abd16dba91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xx}=52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512378} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcdc1dd0-6dd9-55fc-8f56-4c2c1bfe43f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2d81c89-6939-51ba-b7c7-704655922181" :question/math-academy-id "q-251841" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $7$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $2$ | $3$ | $10$ | $9$ | $6$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $15$ | $21$ | $22$ | $23$ | $26$ | $17$ | $16$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{xx}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xx}$ is the sum of the squared deviations of the data ${x}_{i}$ from the mean $\\overset{―}{x},$ that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample mean $\\overset{―}{x}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{2+3+10+9+6+5+7}{7}=6\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{x}$, and their squares.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $2$ | $3$ | $10$ | $9$ | $6$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $15$ | $21$ | $22$ | $23$ | $26$ | $17$ | $16$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})\\,$** | $-4$ | $-3$ | $4$ | $3$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}\\,$** | $16$ | $9$ | $16$ | $9$ | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{xx}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{xx}=16+9+16+9+0+1+1=52.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "714000f9-caea-57a3-a8cb-6b8ec99960d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Variance and Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4fc6b88-f553-5afd-9271-26b9d7dee8c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4fc6b88-f553-5afd-9271-26b9d7dee8c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512692} :answer-field/id #uuid "e373ea2c-9a67-56c0-915f-3067e964017d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac49558f-18ee-5f4d-ae88-d48f8fce7444" :question/math-academy-id "q-251853" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $36$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{36},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{36}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=72,\\,{S}_{yy}=36,\\,{S}_{xy}=54.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, ${\\sigma }_{x}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the variance of ${x}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{x}^{2} & =\\frac{{S}_{xx}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xx}$ is the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${x}_{i}.$\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xx}=72.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{x}^{2} & =\\frac{72}{36} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "714000f9-caea-57a3-a8cb-6b8ec99960d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Variance and Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "308ed413-5640-5680-9536-8532c1207312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "308ed413-5640-5680-9536-8532c1207312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512209} :answer-field/id #uuid "16c3bebc-0c5b-52e0-b178-4898ba483cba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5f1ce794-6e38-5896-94a0-a08e42af5009" :question/math-academy-id "q-251855" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $18$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{18},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{18}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=36,\\,{S}_{yy}=27,\\,{S}_{xy}=30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, ${\\sigma }_{y}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the variance of ${y}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{y}^{2} & =\\frac{{S}_{yy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{yy}$ is the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${y}_{i}.$\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{yy}=27.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{y}^{2} & =\\frac{27}{18} \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "714000f9-caea-57a3-a8cb-6b8ec99960d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Variance and Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a616be15-c64d-5f24-ad7f-1562b756919c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a616be15-c64d-5f24-ad7f-1562b756919c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512492} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4924e73-d6d0-52bf-abba-4d9b0890fbd8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af73b3f9-9505-5255-a05e-b12a6848bab1" :question/math-academy-id "q-251859" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $10$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{10},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{10}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=5,\\,{S}_{yy}=7,\\,{S}_{xy}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, $Cov(x,y)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xy}=6.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{6}{10} \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "714000f9-caea-57a3-a8cb-6b8ec99960d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Variance and Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a5ad1b2-f2c3-5cb5-baa1-6f44df6de444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a5ad1b2-f2c3-5cb5-baa1-6f44df6de444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512425} :answer-field/id #uuid "035cd52a-864b-5a48-b335-680aca817a12" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "783f4f6c-a7ae-5188-a502-9fe2f7c3c94b" :question/math-academy-id "q-251862" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $16$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{16},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{16}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=188,\\,{S}_{yy}=354,\\,{S}_{xy}=212.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, $Cov(x,y)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xy}=212.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{212}{16} \\\\  & =13.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512866 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0afa4d8-6d02-52c6-9836-12089de8f406" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Given a Dataset or Summary Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f1a1d5d-ac93-5fd4-91af-84bb23f04d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512205} {:answer/id #uuid "4df65b77-c79e-5339-86c9-e224a22ee3ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512269} {:answer/id #uuid "4e5c58c7-2283-5a41-b325-74cb1fe7e000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512270} {:answer/id #uuid "54378e41-ed6d-55ce-b916-a2913db68958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512287} {:answer/id #uuid "ac149a28-9c82-50cd-93d4-fcc5ab6e1f18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f1a1d5d-ac93-5fd4-91af-84bb23f04d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xy}=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512205} :answer-field/id #uuid "f815c63a-5ecf-5ce3-b831-33cde02c9d6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "06d00ab5-b798-54f9-9155-cb3b190eccdd" :question/math-academy-id "q-251865" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $6$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $123$ | $122$ | $121$ | $120$ | $125$ | $127$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $102$ | $111$ | $110$ | $105$ | $106$ | $108$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample means $\\overset{―}{x}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{123+122+121+120+125+127}{6}=123\n$$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{102+111+110+105+106+108}{6}=107\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{x}$, ${y}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}$, and their product.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $123$ | $122$ | $121$ | $120$ | $125$ | $127$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $102$ | $111$ | $110$ | $105$ | $106$ | $108$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})\\,$** | $0$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-3$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-5$ | $4$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n| **$\\,({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $0$ | $-4$ | $-6$ | $6$ | $-2$ | $4$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{xy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=0+(-4)+(-6)+6+(-2)+4=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f0ed04b-f011-5818-952d-425a19e0cd5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2dd6fd3-36d2-5d1e-bf27-1912d3b0ed19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "590" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2dd6fd3-36d2-5d1e-bf27-1912d3b0ed19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "590" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512478} :answer-field/id #uuid "101037bb-1cdc-5f57-adda-e1f24aa1b97f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f69f9435-629a-5550-ae7c-8e46c05363dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-251891" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $20$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{20},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{20}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{x}_{i}=400,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{y}_{i}=440, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{x}_{i}^{2}=8\\,590,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{20}{y}_{i}^{2}=9\\,740.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the sum of the squared deviations from the mean for the points ${x}_{i}.$\n\n${S}_{xx}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${x}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & =8\\,590-\\frac{1}{20}(400)^{2} \\\\  & =8\\,590-8\\,000 \\\\  & =590.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512885 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f0ed04b-f011-5818-952d-425a19e0cd5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb82f213-7d9b-508f-8c06-9c2aedb541b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "872" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb82f213-7d9b-508f-8c06-9c2aedb541b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "872" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512705} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2409bc9-7f5e-5536-845e-cd70be80c729" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "42fccfda-10de-5970-a9ed-3564137d6e6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-251893" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $28$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{28},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{28}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{28}{x}_{i}=560,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{28}{y}_{i}=588, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{28}{x}_{i}^{2}=10\\,920,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{28}{y}_{i}^{2}=13\\,220.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the sum of the squared deviations from the mean for the points ${y}_{i}.$\n\n${S}_{yy}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${y}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{yy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i}{y}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{yy} & =13\\,220-\\frac{1}{28}(588)^{2} \\\\  & =13\\,220-12\\,348 \\\\  & =872.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512907 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f0ed04b-f011-5818-952d-425a19e0cd5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c7d59c1-c5ab-558a-8687-f2c12bf613bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xx}=14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512263} {:answer/id #uuid "b4f6e056-c6be-5c14-b14b-419192dbb4aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{xx}=15.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512527} {:answer/id #uu