8+6+9=35.\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i}^{2}=255.$\n\nFinally, by substituting into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{xx}=255-\\frac{1}{5}(35)^{2}=255-245=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f0ed04b-f011-5818-952d-425a19e0cd5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17ecea83-22be-59e1-b8fc-4d9d55c17ca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=74.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512154} {:answer/id #uuid "1f25c884-d1c3-5c38-b1db-3d22ece6160f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=16.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512164} {:answer/id #uuid "28902cf1-3129-5676-a976-7c3efd937418" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512191} {:answer/id #uuid "686321b9-b8b7-5de1-b5a9-b32a7c27a07f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=122" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512350} {:answer/id #uuid "cb01b590-39e9-5aa0-aa3f-5684c3a47e6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28902cf1-3129-5676-a976-7c3efd937418" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512191} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9735c4d-3772-5da2-be56-9a65ca5a65cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d73c45cf-d35a-5a29-81ab-7afc1b61c919" :question/math-academy-id "q-251897" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $14$ | $11$ | $10$ | $9$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $9$ | $5$ | $7$ | $11$ | $8$ |\n\nGiven that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{y}_{i}^{2}=340,$ calculate ${S}_{yy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${y}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{yy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i}{y}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the ${y}_{i}$ data:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{y}_{i}=9+5+7+11+8=40.\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{y}_{i}^{2}=340.$\n\nFinally, by substituting into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{yy}=340-\\frac{1}{5}(40)^{2}=340-320=20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f0ed04b-f011-5818-952d-425a19e0cd5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07bb4a5d-35a3-5032-abeb-6bce7bba7f3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=7.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512120} {:answer/id #uuid "0de895b3-77a8-5886-b1e7-816da0758615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512126} {:answer/id #uuid "96eeb308-1588-5ba3-8348-b5088468fcd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{S}_{yy}=8.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512454} {:answer/id #uuid "acf5f67e-d999-5b95-963c-ed7cce4176da" :answer/ty